{#
    The file manager: folders on the left, the open folder's files on the right (ADR 0020).

    THE FOLDER IS IN THE ADDRESS, so every view of this page is a sendable link and the browser's
    back button works without this page remembering anything. A placeholder could not carry a
    folder tree of arbitrary depth (ADR 0007), which is why it is a query parameter and not a
    path segment — the list carries its own state the same way (ADR 0018).

    TURBO NEEDS NOTHING HERE. Importing it in the layout starts it, so every link below is already
    a Turbo visit: the body is swapped, the page is not rebuilt. That is the whole wiring, and it
    is why this template has no `controllers` map — there is no Stimulus controller on this page.

    NO ADDRESS IS BUILT IN THIS FILE. `FileController` hands every URL over ready-made, the rule
    the list view follows: a template that concatenates URLs is a second place that has to know
    the prefix and the parameter name.

    THE TREE IS OPTIONAL. `tree` is `null` for an editor who may read files but not folders — the
    column is then left out and the file list stays (ADR 0019, additive masking). It is not an
    error state and must not look like one.

    THE ROW FORMS APPEAR WITH THE RIGHTS THEY NEED (003-001-0005). `mayWrite` carries the rename
    field and the move control, `mayDelete` the delete button; without either the row is what it
    was before, a listing. Hiding them is tidiness — `FileController::write()` refuses the post as
    well, which is the part that closes the data.

    MOVING NEEDS THE TREE. Without the right to read folders there is no list to choose a target
    from, so the control is absent even with a write right — the same additive masking as above.

    THE DELETE BUTTON ASKS FIRST, through `data-turbo-confirm`. Turbo is already started by the
    layout, so the confirmation needs no module of its own and no inline script; without Turbo the
    form simply submits, which is why the server asks for the right again.

    THE PREVIEW IS EITHER AN IMAGE OR A LABEL, never an empty box (003-001-0004). `file.preview`
    is an address for the three types a derivative can be made from and `null` for everything
    else; `file.badge` carries the short label those show instead. A file whose preview fails to
    load and a file that was never going to have one must not look the same.

    `loading="lazy"` IS NOT COSMETIC HERE. The core builds a derivative synchronously on first
    request, so a folder of fifty images would otherwise have the browser ask for fifty of them at
    once. Deferring the ones below the fold spreads that over the scrolling instead.

    THE FALLBACK TO THE ORIGINAL IS THE BROWSER'S JOB. Whether the configured alias names an
    existing row cannot be found out from the package (Schema-Vertrag L25), so the derivative is
    simply requested and `admin/file-preview` swaps in `file.original` if it does not arrive.
    Without that module the page is unchanged except that a failed derivative stays a broken
    image — it upgrades the behaviour, it is not what makes previews work.
#}{% extends 'layout.html.twig' %}

{% block bodyAttributes %} class="admin"{% endblock %}

{% macro folderList(items) %}
{% import _self as macros %}
    <ul class="admin-files__tree-list">
{% for item in items %}
        <li class="admin-files__tree-item">
            <a class="admin-files__tree-link{{ item.current ? ' admin-files__tree-link--current' : '' }}"
               href="{{ item.url }}"{{ item.current ? ' aria-current="true"' : '' }}>{{ item.title }}</a>
{% if item.childs is not empty %}
{{ macros.folderList(item.childs) }}
{% endif %}
        </li>
{% endfor %}
    </ul>
{% endmacro %}

{% block content %}
{% import _self as macros %}
<main class="admin__main admin-files">
    <h1>Dateien</h1>

{% if report %}
    <p class="admin-files__report{{ report.ok ? ' admin-files__report--ok' : ' admin-files__report--problem' }}"
       role="status">{{ report.text }}</p>
{% endif %}

    <nav class="admin-files__trail" aria-label="Ordnerpfad">
        <a class="admin-files__trail-link{{ isRoot ? ' admin-files__trail-link--current' : '' }}"
           href="{{ rootUrl }}"{{ isRoot ? ' aria-current="true"' : '' }}>Alle Dateien</a>
{% for step in trail %}
        <span class="admin-files__trail-separator" aria-hidden="true">/</span>
        <a class="admin-files__trail-link{{ step.current ? ' admin-files__trail-link--current' : '' }}"
           href="{{ step.url }}"{{ step.current ? ' aria-current="true"' : '' }}>{{ step.title }}</a>
{% endfor %}
    </nav>

    <div class="admin-files__layout">
{% if tree is not null %}
        <nav class="admin-files__tree" aria-label="Ordner">
            <h2 class="admin-files__tree-heading">Ordner</h2>
{% if tree is empty %}
            <p class="admin-files__empty">Es gibt noch keine Ordner.</p>
{% else %}
{{ macros.folderList(tree) }}
{% endif %}
        </nav>
{% endif %}

        <section class="admin-files__list" aria-label="Dateien">
{% if mayWrite %}
{#
   DIE ZONE STEHT VOR DER LISTE UND AUCH DANN, WENN DER ORDNER LEER IST. Ein leerer Ordner ist
   gerade der Fall, in dem jemand etwas hochladen will — eine Zone, die erst mit der ersten Datei
   erscheint, fehlt genau dann.

   OHNE JAVASCRIPT IST DAS EIN GEWOEHNLICHES FORMULAR, und es funktioniert: Token, Aktion und
   Ordner stehen als Felder darin, die Route nimmt den POST wie jeden anderen Schreibweg an und
   antwortet mit 303. `multiple` bleibt trotzdem stehen — das Modul aus 003-002-0004 braucht es,
   und ohne das Modul kommt bei einer Mehrfachauswahl **eine** Datei an, weil alle Teile denselben
   Feldnamen tragen und PHP nur den letzten behaelt. Weniger als gewuenscht, aber nicht
   stillschweigend falsch.

   `accept` STEHT NUR DA, WENN DAS PROJEKT ES GESETZT HAT (ADR 0021). Ein leerer Default heisst
   kein Attribut — und nicht `accept=""`, was jede Datei ausschliessen wuerde.
#}
            <form class="admin-files__upload" method="post" action="{{ rootUrl }}"
                  enctype="multipart/form-data"
                  data-controller="admin-upload"
                  data-admin-upload-format-field-value="{{ formatField }}"
                  data-admin-upload-format-value="{{ formatJson }}">
                <input type="hidden" name="{{ tokenField }}" value="{{ token }}">
                <input type="hidden" name="{{ actionField }}" value="{{ actions.upload }}">
                <input type="hidden" name="{{ folderField }}" value="{{ folder ?? '' }}">
                <label class="admin-files__upload-label" for="admin-files-upload">
                    Dateien hierher ziehen oder auswählen
                </label>
                <input class="admin-files__upload-input" id="admin-files-upload" type="file"
                       name="{{ uploadField }}" multiple{% if uploadAccept %} accept="{{ uploadAccept }}"{% endif %}
                       data-admin-upload-target="input">
                <button class="admin-files__upload-button" type="submit"
                        data-admin-upload-target="button">Hochladen</button>
                {#
                   BEIDE BEHAELTER STEHEN LEER UND VERSTECKT IM MARKUP, statt vom Modul erzeugt zu
                   werden: so steht der Wortlaut des Hinweises im Template bei allen anderen
                   Saetzen, und das Modul setzt nur `hidden`.
                #}
                <ul class="admin-files__upload-queue" data-admin-upload-target="queue" hidden></ul>
                <p class="admin-files__upload-note" data-admin-upload-target="note" hidden>
                    Die Liste unten zeigt den Stand vor dem Hochladen —
                    <a href="{{ folder is null ? rootUrl : rootUrl ~ '?' ~ folderField ~ '=' ~ folder|url_encode }}">Liste aktualisieren</a>.
                </p>
            </form>
{% endif %}
{% if files is empty %}
            <p class="admin-files__empty">
{% if isRoot %}
                Ausserhalb der Ordner liegt keine Datei.
{% else %}
                Dieser Ordner enthält keine Datei.
{% endif %}
            </p>
{% else %}
            <table class="admin-files__table">
                <thead>
                    <tr>
                        <th scope="col" class="admin-files__cell admin-files__cell--preview">Vorschau</th>
                        <th scope="col" class="admin-files__cell">Name</th>
                        <th scope="col" class="admin-files__cell">Typ</th>
                        <th scope="col" class="admin-files__cell admin-files__cell--size">Größe</th>
{% if mayWrite or mayDelete %}
                        <th scope="col" class="admin-files__cell admin-files__cell--actions">Aktionen</th>
{% endif %}
                    </tr>
                </thead>
                <tbody>
{% for file in files %}
                    <tr class="admin-files__row">
                        <td class="admin-files__cell admin-files__cell--preview">
{% if file.preview %}
                            <img class="admin-files__preview" src="{{ file.preview }}" alt=""
                                 loading="lazy" decoding="async" width="48" height="48"
                                 data-controller="admin-file-preview"
                                 data-admin-file-preview-fallback-value="{{ file.original }}">
{% else %}
                            <span class="admin-files__preview admin-files__preview--badge"
                                  role="img" aria-label="{{ file.type }}">{{ file.badge }}</span>
{% endif %}
                        </td>
                        <td class="admin-files__cell">{{ file.name }}</td>
                        <td class="admin-files__cell">{{ file.type }}</td>
                        <td class="admin-files__cell admin-files__cell--size">{{ file.size }}</td>
{% if mayWrite or mayDelete %}
                        <td class="admin-files__cell admin-files__cell--actions">
{% if mayWrite %}
                            <form class="admin-files__action" method="post" action="{{ rootUrl }}">
                                <input type="hidden" name="{{ tokenField }}" value="{{ token }}">
                                <input type="hidden" name="{{ actionField }}" value="{{ actions.rename }}">
                                <input type="hidden" name="id" value="{{ file.id }}">
                                <input type="hidden" name="{{ folderField }}" value="{{ folder ?? '' }}">
                                <label class="admin-files__action-label" for="name-{{ file.id }}">Name</label>
                                <input class="admin-files__action-input" id="name-{{ file.id }}"
                                       type="text" name="name" value="{{ file.name }}" required>
                                <button class="admin-files__action-button" type="submit">Umbenennen</button>
                            </form>
{% if moveTargets is not null %}
                            <form class="admin-files__action" method="post" action="{{ rootUrl }}">
                                <input type="hidden" name="{{ tokenField }}" value="{{ token }}">
                                <input type="hidden" name="{{ actionField }}" value="{{ actions.move }}">
                                <input type="hidden" name="id" value="{{ file.id }}">
                                <input type="hidden" name="{{ folderField }}" value="{{ folder ?? '' }}">
                                <label class="admin-files__action-label" for="target-{{ file.id }}">Ordner</label>
                                <select class="admin-files__action-select" id="target-{{ file.id }}" name="target">
                                    <option value=""{{ folder is null ? ' selected' : '' }}>(ausserhalb der Ordner)</option>
{% for target in moveTargets %}
                                    <option value="{{ target.id }}"{{ target.id == folder ? ' selected' : '' }}>{{ target.label }}</option>
{% endfor %}
                                </select>
                                <button class="admin-files__action-button" type="submit">Verschieben</button>
                            </form>
{% endif %}
{% endif %}
{% if mayDelete %}
                            <form class="admin-files__action" method="post" action="{{ rootUrl }}"
                                  data-turbo-confirm="„{{ file.name }}“ wirklich löschen? Das lässt sich nicht zurücknehmen.">
                                <input type="hidden" name="{{ tokenField }}" value="{{ token }}">
                                <input type="hidden" name="{{ actionField }}" value="{{ actions.delete }}">
                                <input type="hidden" name="id" value="{{ file.id }}">
                                <input type="hidden" name="{{ folderField }}" value="{{ folder ?? '' }}">
                                <button class="admin-files__action-button admin-files__action-button--danger"
                                        type="submit">Löschen</button>
                            </form>
{% endif %}
                        </td>
{% endif %}
                    </tr>
{% endfor %}
                </tbody>
            </table>

{% if pagination.pages > 1 %}
            <nav class="admin-files__pagination" aria-label="Blättern">
{% if pagination.prevUrl %}
                <a class="admin-files__page-link" rel="prev" href="{{ pagination.prevUrl }}">Zurück</a>
{% endif %}
                <span class="admin-files__page-state">Seite {{ pagination.page }} von {{ pagination.pages }} ({{ pagination.total }} Dateien)</span>
{% if pagination.nextUrl %}
                <a class="admin-files__page-link" rel="next" href="{{ pagination.nextUrl }}">Weiter</a>
{% endif %}
            </nav>
{% endif %}
{% endif %}
        </section>
    </div>
</main>
{% endblock %}
